WEBVTT

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.100
-It's time to contact WSA. -Okay, Glenn.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:05.650
- Calling space authority.

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:10.080
- Space authority, this is spaceship P-1.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:15.800
Spaceship P-1 calling world space authority.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.400
- WSA control, over.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.640
- Please check coordinates.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.360
X, point four.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:28.150
- Y, three point three oh.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:30.000
- Z, zero point zero two.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:37.410
Speed 1000 km/s. We are on course for Planet X in the Scorpion constellation.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:42.740
Time sidereal 23:59 hours 30 seconds. Over.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:48.180
Right. Correct your speed. 005.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:51.810
Corrected speed is 0.005.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:55.890
Good. How are you feeling? You all right?

00:02:55.890 --> 00:03:00.000
We are working and sleeping okay. We would just like to get a little extra.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:29.980
exercise. Well, on planet X, you'll get plenty. Uh, doctor? Yes, Fuji? Is Haruni with you? One second. No, not now. Would you give her a message? Yes. Tell her not to do anything foolish. Foolish? Tell her not to do anything until I can get there. Okay, out. What's so funny?

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.340
- You should have left your sister packed in ice.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:37.110
- Uh, you don't understand.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.960
- Ah, thank you.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:46.290
Did you and Fuji disagree?

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.650
- He treats me like a child.

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:51.080
Always tells me what to do.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.750
Men can always be so unreasonable.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.810
I'm, I'm sorry.

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:58.450
- You don't have to apologize.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.850
someone you like? Fuji doesn't approve? Yes. Oh, we've been looking for you, miss. You've

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:13.670
kept us waiting. I'm so sorry. Doctor, these are the reporters. Oh, yes. I'll come right

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:29.830
in. This friend of yours, what does he do? He's an inventor. Inventor?

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:53.730
good tell me how far away could you hear it hear it you can hear it way down the

00:04:53.730 --> 00:05:00.000
street hey the rest

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.880
I wonder why I can't sell this good idea.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:10.120
I've already turned it off!

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.190
Just a minute!

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:14.430
I wonder who's calling me on the telephone.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:15.430
Thank you.

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:19.630
Okay.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.030
Hello?

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:22.910
Yeah.

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:24.180
This is Tetsui Terry.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.000
What?

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.420
Contract!

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:35.910
Dr. Sakurai, the newly discovered planet is located just beyond the body we know as Jupiter.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.140
Is that correct, sir?

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:38.090
True.

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:39.860
Why wasn't it discovered before?

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:44.690
Planet X is very dark. We cannot observe it with telescopes.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:51.060
The new planet was discovered by Central Observatory while they were tracing strange radio waves.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:59.830
Gentlemen, I can now announce to you that Planet X has been causing our recent magnetic disturbances.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:02.860
Doctor, is there intelligent life on planet X?

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.730
We can't tell yet.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:07.160
It's possible that there is.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:11.180
But the radio waves are not necessarily human.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:14.060
We expect to learn a lot from P1.

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:39.670
Yes?

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:40.880
Isn't this expensive?

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:41.880
Can you afford it?

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:42.960
Sure.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.010
Don't worry.

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:47.160
I sold the invention.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.560
Oh.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:49.380
Really?

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:53.450
Tonight, I get the contract.

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:54.530
Who's taking it?

00:06:54.530 --> 00:07:00.000
An international company, World Education Corporation, a toy manufacturer.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:02.180
Toys. It's no toy.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:05.070
Oh, but...

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:07.900
You are Mr. Terry?

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:09.920
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:14.160
I'm Miss Namakawa from the World Education Corporation.

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:16.160
I'd like to get down to business.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:18.400
We have here our standard contract,

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.920
which calls for payment when your invention is marketed.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:21.980
Is that agreeable?

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:28.030
Oh, sure. Okay?

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:29.500
Oh, yes.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.680
- Is this your wife? - Not yet. She's my girlfriend.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:36.530
Uh, Miss Haruni Fuji.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:38.690
How do you do?

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:41.540
You work at World Space Authority.

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:44.910
And your brother is an astronaut?

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:47.030
Oh, you know my brother?

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:53.300
No, but World Education Corporation is extremely interested in his space activities.

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:54.680
And we're following his trip.

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:04.580
Darling, doesn't it seem odd?

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:05.580
What's odd?

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:11.970
Your invention, giving you $100,000, is it worth that much?

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:15.970
While you and your brother are preoccupied with space, there's money being made here on Earth.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:18.180
You two underrate me. Huh.

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:19.230
Silly.

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:21.240
Your brother thinks I'm a failure.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:25.070
I wish he were here so I could tell him about the $100,000.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:27.020
I'd really stand him on his head.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:29.280
Glenn.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.660
-What's the problem? -Oh, yeah, let's see.

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:37.830
Yep, we're 180 degrees off. My mistake. Sorry, old buddy.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:52.790
And on the other side of it, Planet X.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.180
Planet X, there she is.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:12.070
Space Authority, World Space Authority, this is Spaceship P1, over.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.800
This is Space Authority, go ahead, over.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:18.530
We are now approaching Planet X.

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:20.180
Be very careful.

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:25.100
Yes, sir. After landing, may we act on our own judgment?

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.740
I cannot lead you men by the hand from here.

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:33.100
- Space crew, any questions?

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:33.940
You understand?

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:35.380
- We understand.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.200
You sound like a teenager's father.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:42.270
- Lost contact.

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:54.420
They are now on the blind side of Jupiter.

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:55.540
Do you see anything?

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:08.390
Strange, that blue spot looks like a big grass plane, but maybe it's the sea.

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:11.810
Right, let's get ready. Check your readings.

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:17.310
The radar thermometer is reading 15 degrees.

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:21.730
So far from the sun, that's a high temperature.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:25.480
The universe, nobody knows its secret.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:18.210
- Let's plant the flag on that ridge.

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:20.100
- In the meantime, I'll set up the telemeter.

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:39.220
If gravity is two-thirds of that of the Earth, then the pressure is about half.

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:41.780
That's another surprise.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:02.420
- Are you all right?

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:04.400
- All in order.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.250
- Okay.

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:37.680
On your guard.

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:39.340
Footprints.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:44.810
Glenn, answer.

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:45.790
Hello, Glenn.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:22.720
step into this cylinder.

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:33.040
but I insist that you enter this cylinder without delay.

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:35.060
No, thanks!

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:38.840
I'm sorry, astronaut Fuji, but I must insist.

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:46.100
Your fellow astronaut and your spaceship are here with us,

00:15:46.100 --> 00:15:49.160
so you will step into the cylinder. Please.

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:53.400
All right. All right.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:22.140
Doctor, the contact is now 20 minutes overdue.

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:24.780
Did you check all of the circuits?

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:25.920
Yes, I did, Doctor.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:28.160
Doctor?

00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:36.200
have faith in these men. They are intelligent and well-trained astronauts.

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:48.240
We'll hear from them. They'll call soon. Follow the light. The light is your guide.

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:51.790
- Are you all right, Glenn? - Yeah, you?

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:56.280
- I'm okay. - Gentlemen, remain where you are.

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:29.190
welcome you. Won't you kindly seat yourselves and be comfortable. Controller of Planet

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:36.530
And I've invited you here to discuss something that's very important.

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:39.960
Discuss? Discuss what?

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:42.070
Where's our spaceship?

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:53.240
Don't worry. You can depend upon what I tell you.

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:59.440
A monster again. Zero.

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:06.560
Monster Zero, command all units to take defensive position.

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:08.130
Yes, sir.

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:09.750
What is Monster Zero?

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.680
The demon of our galaxy.

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:19.520
Monster Zero is the reason we cannot live on the surface, but must forever live underground like this.

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:22.720
Alert all units, Monster has begun the attack.

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.680
At what point?

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:28.040
O3M7, O3M7.

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:28.870
All right.

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:34.900
I will show you Monster Zero.

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:46.710
Yes, indeed.

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:52.800
On Earth, you gave this terrifying monster the name of Kidara.

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:55.610
Everything is numbered here.

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:59.830
The monster is zero.

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:12.390
you drive it away if you have an idea how to do it won't you tell us gentlemen we have tried every

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:22.540
force known to us we can't kill him we have failed what are you gonna do now just wait till it goes

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:24.960
away

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:34.180
Moving in at sector 15.

00:20:34.180 --> 00:20:38.010
Move all defensive units into sector 15 and clean it up immediately.

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:49.200
Emergency.

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:51.510
Hydrogen oxide plant has been damaged.

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:54.390
We are to maintain control.

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.490
Something serious must have happened, old buddy.

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:16.160
Yeah, and they don't want us to know about it.

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:19.170
Any country would do the same for secrecy.

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:22.250
Hydrogen oxide?

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:25.370
Hey, hydrogen oxide is water.

00:21:25.570 --> 00:21:26.310
Yeah, it's water.

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:38.410
Ladies, gentlemen, I'm glad to advise you that Monster Zero has now gone.

00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:40.110
What else happened?

00:21:41.390 --> 00:21:44.730
An industrial accident in Sector 15 caused by an oversight.

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:50.110
However, the emergency has now passed, and we are all safe, including you.

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:53.230
Glad to hear that. Now, what else you got to tell?

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:07.600
We need an exterminator, a plan that will destroy King Ghidorah.

00:22:07.600 --> 00:22:16.190
We wish to borrow from you on Earth the Monster Zero-One and Monster Zero-Two, Godzilla and Rodan.

00:22:16.190 --> 00:22:17.840
Are you serious?

00:22:17.840 --> 00:22:21.480
Of course. Deadly serious.

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:27.090
King Ghidorah was driven from Earth, but only by the combined strength of Godzilla and Rodan.

00:22:27.090 --> 00:22:28.450
Will you help us?

00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:38.080
Well, your request is unusual. We don't know how to answer that.

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:41.100
In the first place, we don't even know where Godzilla and Rodan are.

00:22:41.300 --> 00:22:43.520
Even if we did, how would we capture them and bring them here?

00:22:44.380 --> 00:22:48.370
Godzilla is in Japan. He is submerged in Lake Myojin.

00:22:49.110 --> 00:22:54.930
Rodan is a Washigasawa, and we merely seek permission to operate freely on Earth to capture the two demons.

00:22:55.210 --> 00:22:59.410
If Earth will cooperate, we are prepared to pay her.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:04.830
Your medical men on earth have not yet achieved cures for all disease, is that correct?

00:23:04.830 --> 00:23:08.910
Our scientific research is considerably advanced.

00:23:08.910 --> 00:23:14.080
We are prepared therefore to give you a miracle drug that will cure all disease.

00:23:41.290 --> 00:23:46.720
Please explain our desperate need to your people on Earth and help us obtain their cooperation.

00:23:46.720 --> 00:23:52.470
Yes, sir. We'll do our very best. Right, Glenn?

00:23:52.470 --> 00:23:55.220
Condition green. You're cleared for immediate takeoff.

00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:06.370
same journey. Thank you. We're glad we found friends on Planet X. Goodbye till we meet again.

00:24:30.380 --> 00:25:00.000
I think you will agree the report we have just heard.

00:25:00.030 --> 00:25:03.330
from our astronauts is truly amazing.

00:25:03.330 --> 00:25:06.140
On the newly discovered planet,

00:25:06.140 --> 00:25:09.160
there exists a race of superior beings

00:25:09.160 --> 00:25:12.260
with highly advanced scientific knowledge,

00:25:12.260 --> 00:25:13.990
especially in medicine.

00:25:13.990 --> 00:25:17.710
And furthermore, they have extended their hand in friendship

00:25:17.710 --> 00:25:19.290
to the people of the Earth.

00:25:19.290 --> 00:25:23.100
It is our duty, as Supreme Council,

00:25:23.100 --> 00:25:27.710
to carefully study the proposal as set forth by Planet X

00:25:27.710 --> 00:25:29.910
and arrive at an early decision.

00:25:32.780 --> 00:25:40.140
As physicians, my colleagues and I encourage you to agree to give consideration to this

00:25:40.140 --> 00:25:47.340
request for assistance, and our reasoning is as follows: We'll receive a wonder drug.

00:25:47.340 --> 00:25:53.730
Then we can save the people of the earth from suffering, and in time we can eradicate disease.

00:25:53.730 --> 00:26:00.000
The organizations of women have no objection. We acknowledge the sincere message of peace which was

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:02.280
by the controller of the new planet.

00:26:02.280 --> 00:26:07.140
Also, it appears to me that we can learn humanity from these people,

00:26:07.140 --> 00:26:09.440
as well as scientific knowledge.

00:26:09.440 --> 00:26:11.160
Thank you.

00:26:11.160 --> 00:26:14.690
From your remarks, it appears that we are in agreement.

00:26:14.690 --> 00:26:19.810
The Council shall therefore order cooperation with Planet X,

00:26:19.810 --> 00:26:23.630
providing, of course, that the monsters Godzilla and Rodan

00:26:23.630 --> 00:26:25.350
are located where they claim.

00:26:25.350 --> 00:26:29.280
We now have our search units at both locations.

00:27:05.690 --> 00:27:10.580
- Mr. Terry? - Yes?

00:27:10.580 --> 00:27:14.080
Miss Namakawa's out of town. I wonder if I could help you.

00:27:14.080 --> 00:27:20.550
Uh, I'd like to know what you're doing with my invention.

00:27:20.550 --> 00:27:21.930
The Lady Guard alarm.

00:27:21.930 --> 00:27:24.510
Uh, we're still studying that item.

00:27:24.510 --> 00:27:28.180
Still studying it? You say that every time I ask.

00:27:28.180 --> 00:27:29.860
Who's in charge here?

00:27:36.940 --> 00:27:38.870
-Pardon me, sir? -Has he gone?

00:27:38.870 --> 00:27:42.080
No. He wants to know what we're going to do.

00:27:42.080 --> 00:27:55.820
He's persistent. Go get rid of him politely.

00:27:55.820 --> 00:27:57.300
Anderson Fenton...

00:28:05.310 --> 00:28:08.240
- Tetsui, my brother is waiting, let's hurry.

00:28:08.240 --> 00:28:10.420
- I sure don't feel like seeing him.

00:28:10.420 --> 00:28:12.450
- Don't say that, darling.

00:28:12.450 --> 00:28:13.520
Cheer up.

00:28:13.520 --> 00:28:16.090
I want you to make a good impression on him today.

00:28:16.090 --> 00:28:18.250
- Your sister's late, huh?

00:28:18.250 --> 00:28:20.340
- Yeah, she's always late.

00:28:20.340 --> 00:28:23.360
- So you can't forgive the guy who stole her heart?

00:28:23.360 --> 00:28:25.050
- Coffee. - Yes, sir.

00:28:25.050 --> 00:28:27.120
- Do you have something else to do?

00:28:27.120 --> 00:28:28.420
- Actually, I'm waiting for someone myself.

00:28:28.420 --> 00:28:29.480
We're going on a drive.

00:28:30.440 --> 00:28:34.050
Japanese girl? Not the wrong kind, I hope.

00:28:34.050 --> 00:28:36.740
You had to check up on a girl's past every time you went on a date.

00:28:36.740 --> 00:28:39.870
You'd never fall in love.

00:28:39.870 --> 00:28:42.150
Speaking of checking out something,

00:28:42.150 --> 00:28:45.790
you can't forget about that damaged H2O plant.

00:28:45.790 --> 00:28:48.390
I think Planet X is very short of water.

00:28:48.390 --> 00:28:51.150
Yes, I do too.

00:28:51.150 --> 00:28:57.750
And, Glenn, I don't know exactly how much or how far we can trust them.

00:29:00.160 --> 00:29:01.580
Hello. Are we late?

00:29:01.700 --> 00:29:02.380
Yes, you are.

00:29:02.850 --> 00:29:04.250
Good afternoon, Glenn.

00:29:04.470 --> 00:29:04.670
Hi.

00:29:05.140 --> 00:29:05.640
Shall we?

00:29:11.130 --> 00:29:19.160
Terry, you've had good news.

00:29:19.690 --> 00:29:20.990
Sold one of your inventions, huh?

00:29:22.220 --> 00:29:22.720
Yes, sir.

00:29:22.990 --> 00:29:23.310
Good.

00:29:24.800 --> 00:29:25.980
But I can't understand.

00:29:27.300 --> 00:29:30.000
Why should a company pay so much money for a simple idea?

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:36.820
like that. I haven't gotten anything yet. That's what I thought. Terry, I think a great deal of my

00:29:36.820 --> 00:29:43.950
sister, and I don't know whether you can make her happy. I know. You don't have to agree with him

00:29:43.950 --> 00:29:51.720
like that. What do you think? We have mutual trust in each other. Isn't that the most important thing?

00:29:51.720 --> 00:29:56.780
I think so. Mutual trust is a beautiful thing. Oh, Glenn, you don't know what you're saying. Oh,

00:29:56.780 --> 00:29:59.760
no, I just stated a general fact. That won't buy groceries.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:01.780
Oh, true, but it's necessary in everyday life.

00:30:01.800 --> 00:30:02.520
You're fighting me.

00:30:02.910 --> 00:30:04.370
You always agree with the girls.

00:30:05.990 --> 00:30:07.230
Well, if you'll excuse me.

00:30:07.370 --> 00:30:09.260
Oh, do you have to go?

00:30:09.460 --> 00:30:10.320
Yep, I've got a date.

00:30:11.560 --> 00:30:13.000
The enemy is very powerful.

00:30:13.120 --> 00:30:14.480
You better do something spectacular.

00:30:14.480 --> 00:30:14.820
Yeah.

00:30:31.850 --> 00:30:34.360
Oh, Miss Namakawa.

00:30:34.360 --> 00:30:36.530
Oh?

00:30:36.530 --> 00:30:39.780
Hi, baby.

